1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Scan vial, cap, sterile pod, blister pack, syringe, and dose dial.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Visual-servo approach uses the learned tactile residual policy.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Five fingers close and tactile contacts stabilize the vial.

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,000
In-hand cap rotation exceeds 200 degrees without losing the vial.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The hold survives a 4N lateral shove and a 9x load challenge.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,000
A lateral slip disturbance is recovered under 1.2 millimeters.

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The vial is delivered to the sterile pod and verified.

8
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
The audit button is pressed after delivery.

9
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
A blister pill is pressed from its pack.

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
The syringe plunger is dosed with two-finger control.

11
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The dose dial is turned to confirm the care sequence.

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Metrics, stress replay, and policy card are exported.
